    <string name="classification_automatic">Automatic detection</string>
    <string name="calibration_edge_case_note">Calibration can help on vertically folding devices whose inner display is under 600 dp, after display-size changes, or when a manufacturer reports unusual configuration values.</string>
    <string name="usage_access_disclosure_title">How usage data is handled</string>
    <string name="usage_access_disclosure_body">To calculate outer- and inner-display usage, Foldlytics reads displayed app names, screen on and lock state, screen configuration, and their timestamps. It also reads this data about every six hours while the app is closed and stores it in an on-device database until you uninstall the app.\n\nThe data is used only for statistics and for CSV export or sharing that you initiate. It is not used for advertising or third-party analytics and is not transmitted automatically. Only when you choose to export or share is the data passed to the destination or app you select.</string>
    <string name="usage_access_required_title">Usage access is required</string>
    <string name="usage_access_required_body">App display time and fold state are calculated only on this device.</string>
    <string name="calibration_values_title">Device-specific detection values</string>
    <string name="calibration_instructions">Close the device and record the outer display, then open it and record the inner display. Automatic detection remains active until both values are saved.</string>
    <string name="calibration_configuration_unavailable">The current display size could not be read. Wait for the screen to settle, then record it again.</string>
    <string name="calibration_anchors_too_close">The outer and inner measurements are too similar to tell apart. Fully close or open the device, then record the correct display again.</string>

